  "notes": [
    "How it works: a free-for-all against bots in Mirrorwarfare's own engine, which loads MW2 (2009) maps and guns from your install and adds Mirror's Edge Catalyst parkour: wallruns, vaults, slides and ledge grabs on the Parkour Playground arena.",
    "Press Play: the app starts iw4l.exe from your MW2 folder (not MW2 itself) straight into the Parkour Playground with 7 bots. By hand: run iw4l.exe there with map mec:testbox --cmds \"wait world; bot add 7\" (\"bot add 0\" to practise alone). Never start MW2 from Steam for this.",
    "Controls: W runs (speed builds over about 3 s, no sprint key), Space jumps, wallruns, wallclimbs, vaults and grabs ledges, C slides and rolls, Q turns 180 degrees, mouse fires MW2 weapons (R reload, V melee, F/G grenades). Type thirdperson in the console (~) to watch the body.",
    "You need Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 2 (2009) multiplayer installed through Steam; Windows only. Mirror's Edge Catalyst is optional: upstream's tools\\mec\\setup.ps1 (about 45 GB free) extracts Faith's animations and city arenas from your own copy; without it stock MW2 animations are used.",
    "Offline against bots, or private matches on iw4L's own servers; it never touches official MW2 servers. Only free-for-all is tuned, bots find parkour routes by trial, third person is not fully 1:1, and online play between machines is untested.",
    "Restore removes iw4l.exe, the arena and the licenses but leaves the iw4l-artifacts folder (logs, caches) in the MW2 folder: delete it by hand if you want. Beta: report bugs to the author with the Report a bug link."
  ]
